  "notes": "FORMS: {怪|あや}しく (adverbial), {怪|あや}しさ (noun form).\n\nSense 1 covers people, behavior, and situations that arouse suspicion. Sense 2 covers things that are unreliable or of questionable quality — often used for weather, skills, or claims.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {怪|あや}しい{人|ひと} — suspicious person\n- {怪|あや}しい{動|うご}き — suspicious movement\n- {怪|あや}しい{雲行|くもゆ}き — ominous clouds; uncertain outlook\n- {日本語|にほんご}が{怪|あや}しい — one's Japanese is shaky\n\nSIMILAR WORDS: {疑|うたが}わしい focuses on doubt or disbelief, while {怪|あや}しい carries a nuance of something being creepy, off, or unreliable.",
